{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1. Inspect a surface, get its trace",
  "description": "Follow the repaired demo candidate from local data to a keyboard- and touch-reachable Trace Lens. Run npm run happy-path and npm run dev first. Final UI acceptance remains pending.",
  "ref": "main",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "index.html",
      "line": 11,
      "description": "One page and one React entrypoint. The demo synchronizes its detail selection with URL parameters; installed hosts retain their own routing."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/main.tsx",
      "line": 6,
      "description": "One React root mounts DemoDashboard. The browser reads a prepared local dataset; it does not open SQLite or start an agent."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/demoState.ts",
      "line": 31,
      "description": "The demo fetches public JSON with an AbortSignal, checks HTTP status, limits the body to 1 MiB and validates required render fields with Zod. DemoContent supplies a ten-second timeout and visible retry."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/DemoDashboard.tsx",
      "line": 147,
      "description": "A normal Inspect trace button calls the existing useTraceLens().openHit API. Keyboard and touch users have a visible entrypoint; hosts can add their own controls with the same API. Historical D4 is repaired in this candidate, pending final judge."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/trace/TraceLensProvider.tsx",
      "line": 58,
      "description": "The existing Ctrl/Cmd-click shortcut still resolves a tagged region through one window listener. It complements normal controls; it is not the only entrypoint. Ordinary clicks on host content pass through."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/trace/TraceLensProvider.tsx",
      "line": 15,
      "description": "The DOM event becomes a SurfaceHit: one required surface id and three optional reference strings. No DOM node crosses. Both data-nodetrace-surface and data-noderoom-surface are supported. This identifies a selection; it does not grant authority."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/trace/types.ts",
      "line": 10,
      "description": "SurfaceHit is the value hosts pass to openHit: surfaceId plus optional artifactId, elementId and targetRef."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/trace/TraceLensPanel.tsx",
      "line": 30,
      "description": "An unregistered selection now opens Surface unavailable with missing-data guidance. It does not fabricate a registry entry or proof. Historical D1 is repaired in this candidate, pending final judge."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/trace/TraceLensPanel.tsx",
      "line": 21,
      "description": "The native dialog makes the page behind it inert. The panel focuses Close, wraps Tab between its controls, and restores the opener on dismissal. Escape, Close and a pointer gesture that starts and ends on the backdrop dismiss it."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/trace/TraceLensPanel.tsx",
      "line": 184,
      "description": "Exact element/artifact matches take priority; absent matches fall back to the surrounding surface. The panel says this does not verify the exact element. Proof and runtime windows remain bounded to six rows each."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/demoNavigation.ts",
      "line": 31,
      "description": "Only the demo owns step, tab and lens URL parameters. Reload and history restore selection after state is ready; invalid steps normalize against the loaded dataset. No URL parameter grants builder access."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/trace/TraceLensPanel.tsx",
      "line": 124,
      "description": "The portable panel renders ownership only with builder capability, Builder mode and a matching ownership row. Hosts must derive capability from server-verified identity and serve a safe projection."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/demoState.ts",
      "line": 59,
      "description": "Public JSON is data, not builder authority. The demo discards privileged flags and ownership and always mounts its provider in Review mode. A producer-side environment flag is not authentication."
    },
    {
      "file": "scripts/init-sqlite.mjs",
      "line": 222,
      "description": "The seed producer normally omits ownership. Its NODETRACE_BUILDER_CAPABLE option can export internal rows, so operators must not publish a privileged export as a public file. Installed hosts own their privileged server route."
    }
  ]
}
